# Navigation & presentation wiring

Full write-up (read before non-trivial changes): `.claude/skills/navigation-presentation/SKILL.md`.

View models derive from `PresentationModelBase<TInput, TResult>` and are
`[AddINotifyPropertyChangedInterface]`. Views derive from
`PresenterUserControl<TViewModel, TInput, TResult>`; the constructor calls
`InitializeComponent()` and nothing else.

## Two navigation mechanisms — know which you are in

1. **`NavigationController.PushAsync`** (framework) — only the outer flow:
   `App.OnFrameworkInitializationCompleted` installs `ShellWindow`/`ShellView`
   and pushes `LoginViewModel`; login pushes `MainViewModel`.
2. **`CurrentView`** (`Viewmodels/Session/CurrentView.cs`) — everything inside
   the shell. `MainView` binds a `TransitioningContentControl` to
   `CurrentView.ViewShown`; tabs and detail screens are swapped by assigning it.

`CurrentView` keeps a **back stack**: `ViewShown = x` pushes+shows (drill-in);
`ShowRoot(x)` clears the stack (the five tabs); `GoBack()` pops (so a service
opened from a tutor returns to that tutor, while the tutor's own Back reaches the
tutors list).

## The gotcha

A screen shown through `CurrentView` is **never `RunAsync`'d**, so
`OnRunStarting`/`OnRunFinishing` never fire. Those view models expose a public
`ReloadAsync()` and the view calls it from `OnLoaded` in code-behind — the one
sanctioned exception to "code-behind is initialization only". Follow it for any
new screen reached this way.

## Passing "which record am I opening"

`Factory.Create()` takes no runtime args, so the selection is set on
`AppSession` immediately before the assignment (`SelectedDogId`,
`SelectedTutorId`, `SelectedServiceId`, `SelectedServiceKind`). **Keep the
set-then-show pair adjacent** so it stays greppable. `AppSession` also carries
the signed-in sitter, the `DataChanged`/`LogoutRequested` events, and the shared
formatters (`TypeLabel`, `Money`, `DateTimeLabel`, `TimeLabel`, `Initials`).

Commands are `SynchronizedCommand(..., SynchronizationBehavior.Discard, true)`.
Rows that own commands (`ServiceRow`, `FutureServiceRow`, `TutorFutureServiceRow`)
are `IDisposable`; the owning list disposes them on rebuild — follow that rather
than leaking a command per row per refresh.

Related: `styling-design-canvas` (screens shown via `CurrentView` must not add
their own `DesignCanvas`).
